<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01268#religious_identity_display> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The visual markers (kippah and hijab) are used to signal the religious identity of the individuals as Muslim. This is not explicitly stated in the text but is a key element in understanding the cultural context of the image. The display of religious identity in a domestic, affectionate setting is often used to promote a positive image of religious practice and family life, countering stereotypes or misconceptions about religion."@en .
