<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01268#social_media_engagement_tactic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The text 'like and share if you agree' is a common social media engagement tactic designed to encourage user interaction, virality, and community building. It leverages social proof and emotional resonance to prompt users to participate, often by sharing content that aligns with their values or beliefs. This tactic is not visible in the image but is essential to understanding the meme's function."@en .
