<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01268#muslim_family_bonding_stereotype> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The image and text promote a positive, idealized stereotype of Muslim families, emphasizing intergenerational love and cultural pride. This stereotype is often used in media and social content to counteract negative portrayals of Muslims, portraying them as loving, family-oriented, and culturally cohesive. The visual markers (kippah, hijab) combined with the affectionate embrace are used to reinforce this positive cultural narrative."@en .
